                            <comment id="16185077" author="vitaliyb" created="Thu, 28 Sep 2017 23:05:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;, please take a look.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16187982" author="agura" created="Mon, 2 Oct 2017 12:42:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=VitaliyB&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;VitaliyB&quot;&gt;VitaliyB&lt;/a&gt; I&apos;ve looked to your changes and don&apos;t see relation between changes and description. At first sight only txs order is changed in &lt;tt&gt;txLockInfos&lt;/tt&gt; method. From my point of view it shouldn&apos;t affect the result. It would be great if you provide reproducer/tests that fails without fix and doesn&apos;t fail after fix?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16187997" author="vitaliyb" created="Mon, 2 Oct 2017 13:19:32 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agura&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agura&quot;&gt;agura&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://reviews.ignite.apache.org/ignite/review/IGNT-CR-355?filePath=/modules/core/src/test/java/org/apache/ignite/internal/processors/cache/transactions/TxOptimisticDeadlockDetectionTest.java&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;Upsource Test&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
TxOptimisticDeadlockDetectionTest#testDeadlocksPartitionedNearTxOnPrimary in my commit reproduce this bug with a probability of 99%(based on HashMap order).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;GridNearTxLocal and GridDhtTxLocal can contain different entries for the same key. And these entries are associated with different MVCC candidates. &lt;br/&gt;
If GridNearTxLocal processed first, required MVCC candidates can be skipped.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (res.txLocks(txKey) == &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;) {
.
.
.
}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
